### IPP-1722 Coding progress in the full backup
### Before: import problems (npm run import:problems -- javascript --yes) and Submit at least one problem while logged in.
### Put ADMIN_PASSWORD while testing, then CHANGE_ME back.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@adminEmail = askedin143@gmail.com
@adminPassword = changeme
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}


### 1. Admin login -> 200
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }


### 2. Full export -> backup.problemProgress is a list: [{ user (email), language "javascript", problem (slug),
###    submits, fails, solved, solvedAt, code, createdAt, updatedAt }]
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export?scope=full
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 3. Content-only export -> NO problemProgress (no personal data)
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/export?scope=content
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### 4. Dry run with a small file -> problemProgress { added 0, existing 1, skipped 1 } (your own row exists; "no-such" problem skipped)
###    and errors has 'problem not found (run npm run import:problems ...)'
###    Change "user" to your admin email and "problem" to a problem you submitted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/backup/import?dryRun=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "problemProgress": [
    { "user": "askedin143@gmail.com", "language": "javascript", "problem": "count-vowels", "submits": 1, "fails": 0, "solved": true },
    { "user": "askedin143@gmail.com", "language": "javascript", "problem": "no-such", "submits": 1 }
  ]
}

### 5. Admin -> Backup page: "Download full backup" shows "..., N coding progress rows";
###    choosing that file shows a "Coding progress" box in the check result.
